                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The difference between this and its remaster Link Evolution is very important: Base Legacy (this game) uses [b] a different, older ruleset [/b] from Link Evolution. If you're exclusively familiar with the way YGO used to work, from the ARC-V (Pendulum) days and prior, I think either this or the retro collection are your best shots. However, Link Evolution is objectively a more complete experience. If you are familiar with modern Dueling, it will offer almost 3000 additional cards, all of this game's content and DLC, as well as early VRAINS (Link) cards.\n\nTlDr: if you're more familiar with older YGO, and particularly with the anime, this is a serviceable simulator for the Pendulum-and-older rules. I do recommend it for those demographics. However, if you are looking for ARC-V (incomplete here) and VRAINS (missing entirely) content - or a more complete singleplayer Dueling sim - just go for Link Evolution. Especially on a sale, I'm not too terribly pissed about finding this out now.",
